<h1 id="anexo-i-condiciones-específicas-del-nivel-básico"><strong>Annex I — Specific Conditions of the Basic Level </strong></h1>
<details>
<summary><strong>See Annex I </strong></summary>
<ol type="1">
<li>
<p><strong>Applicability </strong></p>
<p>This Annex I will apply when the Adhering Entity, having signed the Framework Contract,
                subscribe this Annex I and obtain authorization to hold the Participation Level of <strong>Basic Level </strong>on the ISBE network, in accordance with the <strong>Policy ECO1010 – Policy for joining and exiting the ISBE ecosystem </strong>.
            </p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Purpose of the Annex </strong></p>
<p>The purpose of this Annex I is to establish the particular conditions under which the Level
                Basic accesses and uses ISBE infrastructure and services at a limited operational level and
                non-intrusive, without operation of its own nodes and without direct interaction with the <em>blockchain </em>to
                margin of the flows enabled and supervised by ISBE. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Qualification as Basic Level </strong></p>
<p>The Adhering Entity will hold the Basic Participation Level while the Contract is in force.
                Framework and this Annex I and meets, at all times, the specific requirements for admission and
                permanence associated with this Level of Participation that are established in the <strong>Policy ECO1010 – Policy for joining and exiting the ISBE ecosystem </strong>and in the
                other ISBE Policies that are applicable to you, including, in particular, the obligations of
                updating of information and management of identities provided for in the <strong>Policy INF1050 – Digital identities, credentials and management policy
                    access </strong>.
            </p>
<p>The Managing Entity may periodically review compliance with these requirements and, where appropriate,
                reconsider qualification as a Basic Participant in accordance with the Framework Agreement and the <strong>Policy ECO1010 – Policy for joining and exiting the ISBE ecosystem </strong>.
            </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Basic Level functional capabilities </p>
<p>In its capacity as Basic Level, the Adhering Entity may, in the terms and with the limits
                established in the ISBE Policies that are applicable, in particular the <strong>ECO1020 Policy – ​​Use Case and SC Management Policy </strong>and the <strong>ECO1030 Policy – ​​SCs pausing/locking/data deletion policy </strong>:
            </p>
<ol type="a">
<li>
<p>Access the private area and the ISBE portal, including documentation, manuals,
                        communications, operational notices and other content that the Managing Entity makes available
                        of ecosystem participants. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Use libraries, assistants and <em>wizards </em>of <em>Smart Contracts </em>preconfigured
                        that ISBE offers in a non-programmatic and supervised deployment mode, always through
                        authorized flows and tools without direct access to network nodes, in accordance with the <strong>ECO1020 Policy – ​​Use Case and SC Management Policy </strong>.
                    </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Access, when enabled, basic notarization services, registration of
                        evidence and time stamping on the ISBE infrastructure, in the terms established by the <strong>ECO1020 Policy – ​​Use Case and SC Management Policy </strong>and with the
                        data protection precautions <strong>Policy NOR1060 – Personal data protection policy </strong>.
                    </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Access and use the common support and communication elements of the ISBE ecosystem,
                        including, at a minimum: <strong><em>(Yo) </em></strong>access to helpdesk channels and
                        other enabled support services; and <strong><em>(ii) </em></strong>the reception of
                        official notifications and operational communications through the ISBE Private Area,
                        so that even Adhering Entities without advanced technological functions have access to
                        adequate assistance, transparency and compliance mechanisms. Likewise, the Basic Level
                        may include access to an internal and controlled token distribution mechanism
                        operational ( <em>faucet </em>or equivalent system), intended exclusively to provide the
                        gas strictly necessary for the execution of authorized operations, in accordance
                        with the ISBE Policies and, where applicable, with the <strong>Policy ADM1010 – Fees and remuneration policy </strong>, without this implying
                        access to external markets or the configuration of an investment instrument or of a
                        speculative. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Formulate queries, requests and, where appropriate, proposals for evolution towards other Levels of
                        Participation through the channels defined in the <strong>Policy ECO1010 – Policy for joining and exiting the ISBE ecosystem </strong>.
                    </p>
</li>
</ol>
<p>In no case does the Basic Participation Level enable, by itself, to operate network nodes
                ISBE or to expose the node's own infrastructure, which will require the assumption, if applicable, of the
                Levels of Execution Node Operator and/or Consensus Node Operator through the annexes
                corresponding. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Specific obligations of the Basic Level </strong></p>
<p>Without prejudice to the general obligations assumed in the Framework Contract and the ISBE Policies that
                applicable to it, the Basic Level undertakes, in particular, to: </p>
<ol type="a">
<li>
<p>Use the infrastructure, private area and ISBE services exclusively for the
                        lawful and proper purposes of its activity, respecting at all times the <strong>Policy NOR1020 – Organizational Liability Regime Policy </strong>,
                        the <strong>Policy NOR1030 – Code of Ethics </strong>, the <strong>Policy NOR1040 – Conflict of Interest Policy </strong>, the <strong>Policy NOR1080 – Competition and neutrality policy </strong>and the <strong>Policy NOR1090 – Environmental Sustainability Policy </strong>.
                    </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Comply with the confidentiality obligations provided for in the Framework Contract and in the <strong>Policy NOR1050 – Confidentiality Policy </strong>, in relation to any
                        non-public information that you access through the ISBE portal or services. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Process personal data in accordance with the <strong>Policy NOR1060 – Personal data protection policy </strong>, minimizing the
                        inclusion of personal data in any functionality that may generate records about the
                        ISBE infrastructure and prioritizing the use of hash mechanisms, references or pseudonymization
                        when provided for in the ISBE Policies and, in particular, the <strong>ECO1030 Policy – ​​SCs pausing/locking/data deletion policy </strong>.
                    </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Respect intellectual property rights and the licensing regime defined in the <strong>Policy NOR1070 – Intellectual Property Policy </strong>, especially in
                        related to the use of documentation, libraries, templates, wizards and other assets made available to you
                        provision by ISBE. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Manage access credentials, certificates, API <em>Keys </em>or other mechanisms
                        authentication and authorization in accordance with the <strong>Policy INF1050 – Digital identities, credentials and management policy
                            access </strong>, guaranteeing its custody, diligent use and non-assignment to third parties.
                        authorized. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Use the <em>wizards </em>, bookstores and notarization or registration services only to
                        through the channels and flows approved by the Managing Entity, refraining from attempting
                        circumvent such flows or interact directly with nodes or infrastructure layers to which
                        that you are not authorized to access. </p>
<p>When the Adhering Entity uses the <em>wizards </em>or deployment assistants <em>Smart Contracts </em>associated with the Basic Level to generate assets or instruments <em>on-chain </em>of a transferable nature (including, but not limited to,
                        tokens issued in a Use Case network), you must keep and maintain a record <em>off-chain </em>, minimum, truthful and updated of the entities or people to whom you deliver
                        said assets within the framework of the primary issue, in the terms and with the scope provided
                        in the ISBE Policies, in particular in the <strong>ECO1020 Policy – ​​Use Case and SC Management Policy </strong>, without prejudice to
                        what is provided in the <strong>Policy NOR1060 – Personal data protection policy </strong>regarding the
                        data that, if applicable, are incorporated into said registry. Said registry will have exclusively
                        purpose of basic traceability and reinforcement of the responsibility of the issuer and the
                        coherence of the ecosystem, and will not in itself constitute an identification procedure,
                        due diligence or comprehensive compliance regarding the prevention of money laundering or
                        financing of terrorism. The Adherent Entity will not be obliged, by virtue of this
                        Framework Contract, to identify secondary owners or to supervise transmissions
                        subsequent transactions of assets issued between third parties. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p>Attend to the communications and operational notices that the Managing Entity disseminates through the
                        portal or other enabled channels, implementing within a reasonable period of time the measures that, in
                        If applicable, are required to maintain adequate use and in accordance with the ISBE Policies. </p>
</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Economic conditions </strong></p>
<p>The quotas, fees, rates or other economic conditions associated with the Participation Level
                Basic will be governed entirely by what is established by the <strong>Policy ADM1010 – Fees and remuneration policy </strong>, in its current version in
                every moment. </p>
<p>Failure to pay the appropriate amounts may constitute a relevant non-compliance and
                enable the Managing Entity to adopt the measures provided for in the Framework Contract and in the <strong>Policy ECO1010 – Policy for joining and exiting the ISBE ecosystem </strong>,
                including, where appropriate, the suspension of services and forced withdrawal from the ISBE ecosystem. </p>
</li>
<li>
<p><strong>Termination or modification of the Basic Participation Level </strong></p>
<p>Voluntary withdrawal, revocation or any other form of termination of the Participation Level
                Basic will be governed by the provisions of the Framework Contract and the <strong>Policy ECO1010 – Policy for joining and exiting the ISBE ecosystem </strong>. The
                Termination of this Annex I will not in itself entail the termination of the Framework Contract while the
                Adherent Entity maintains at least another Participation Level in force. </p>
</li>
<li>
